id: SEC-034
title: Overly permissive file permissions (CWE-732)
category: security
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .py .js .ts .rb .java .go
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
patterns:
  - regex: (?:os\.chmod|chmod|fs\.chmod|File\.chmod).*0?o?777
    message: "World-writable file permissions (777) — any user can read/write/execute"
  - regex: (?:os\.chmod|chmod|fs\.chmod|File\.chmod).*0?o?666
    message: "World-writable file permissions (666) — any user can read/write"
fix: Use minimal permissions (0644 for files, 0755 for directories). Never use 777/666.